<!DOCTYPE topic
        SYSTEM "https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/xhtml-entities.dtd">
<topic xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
       xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://resources.jetbrains.com/writerside/1.0/topic.v2.xsd"
       title="AZD: What's new" id="Azd-Whats-New">

    <primary-label ref="azd"/>
    <show-structure for="chapter" depth="2"/>

    <link-summary>Notable changes in the AZD 2026.3, 2026.2 and 2026.1 release lines.</link-summary>
    <card-summary>New features and notable fixes in recent AZD releases.</card-summary>
    <web-summary>What's new in AZD, the Azure DevOps plugin for JetBrains IDEs: pull request review, sign-in,
        pipelines, approvals, Boards and AI changes in recent releases.</web-summary>

    <p>
        This page lists notable changes by release line, newest first.
        Each release line targets one IDE version; for example, AZD 2026.3 runs on IDEs 2026.3.
        For every release, see the
        <a href="https://plugins.jetbrains.com/plugin/22319-azd/versions">version history on JetBrains Marketplace</a>.
    </p>

    <chapter title="AZD 2026.3" id="azd-2026-3">
        <chapter title="IDE support" id="platform-support">
            <p>
                AZD 2026.3 runs only on JetBrains IDEs 2026.3 (build 263).
                The latest release, 2026.3.6, needs build 263.5153 or later.
                IDEs 2026.2 stay on AZD 2026.2.23, the final release for that IDE version.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Pull request review" id="pr-review-improvements">
            <p>AZD 2026.3.6 makes the state of a pull request easier to read in the <a href="Pull-Request-Details.topic">details panel</a>:</p>
            <list>
                <li>Reviewer rows show rejected, waiting for author and approved with suggestions separately.</li>
                <li>A reviewer who declined to review is shown as declined.</li>
                <li>A pull request whose merge Azure DevOps is still evaluating says so.</li>
                <li>A merge blocked by a branch policy is explained in the details panel.</li>
                <li>The unresolved-comments row links to the comments.</li>
                <li>The branch popup can open a pull request in a new Git worktree.</li>
            </list>
            <p>
                Fixes in this release: linking a work item reports failures, a newly opened pull request is no longer listed as unmergeable,
                and refreshing pull requests, pipelines or boards no longer crashes on recent 2026.3 builds.
            </p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="AZD 2026.2" id="new-in-2026-2">
        <list>
            <li><b>Awaiting My Vote filter:</b> a quick filter in the <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic">pull request list</a>
                shows pull requests assigned to you that you have not voted on yet.</li>
            <li><b>Zoomable comment images:</b> click an image in a pull request comment to open it in an editor tab.</li>
            <li><b>Viewed state for deleted and moved files:</b> deleted and moved files in a pull request can be marked as viewed.</li>
            <li><b>Per-pipeline approval muting:</b> mute approval notifications for one pipeline from the notification or from
                <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Approvals.topic" anchor="mute-approvals">Pipeline Settings</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Richer run list:</b> runs show their commit message, and run details show a colored status label.
                Runs on the default branch link to the pull request that triggered them.</li>
            <li><b>Boards:</b> open the <a href="Azd-Boards.topic" anchor="kanban-board">Kanban board</a> of any project in the organization,
                and filter work items by iteration, including <code>@CurrentIteration</code>.</li>
            <li><b>Pipeline metrics:</b> new <control>Top Failure Causes</control> and <control>Slowest Stages</control> widgets in
                <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Metrics.topic"/>.</li>
            <li><b>Default AI provider notice:</b> a notification at startup explains that AI features use the built-in AZD cloud provider by default,
                with a link to the AI settings.</li>
            <li><b>Optional task integration:</b> AZD loads without the Issue Trackers plugin (formerly Task Management), which is no longer bundled with every IDE.
                Only the <a href="Azd-Boards.topic" anchor="tasks-integration">task server integration</a> needs it.</li>
        </list>
        <p>
            Performance and reliability: watching a long-running build uses less memory, large test result lists sort and filter faster,
            opening Settings no longer freezes the IDE, and views that need the built-in browser explain why when it is not available.
            Completed pull requests show their changed, binary, renamed and deleted files.
        </p>

        <chapter title="AI models" id="enhanced-ai">
            <p>
                AZD 2026.2.23 added newer OpenAI, Claude and Gemini models to the AI settings.
                Providers set to a retired Gemini model move to its successor.
                See <a href="Azd-AI.topic" anchor="ai-providers">AI providers</a>.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Sign-in reliability" id="ui-improvements">
            <p>
                Since AZD 2026.2.21, Microsoft Entra ID and Azure CLI sign-in no longer stop working after about an hour.
                A sign-in error now offers a <control>Log in again…</control> button instead of needing an IDE restart.
            </p>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="AZD 2026.1" id="azd-2026-1">
        <list>
            <li><b>Sign in with Microsoft:</b> OAuth sign-in with Microsoft Entra ID for Azure DevOps Services, from the tool windows, the clone dialog and Settings.
                See <a href="Azd-Installation.topic" anchor="azd-oauth-login">Sign in with Microsoft</a>.</li>
            <li><b>Sign in with Azure CLI:</b> for organizations that block OAuth apps or phase out personal access tokens.
                See <a href="Azd-Installation.topic" anchor="azd-azcli-login">Sign in with Azure CLI</a>.</li>
            <li><b>AZD Boards tool window:</b> find, edit and create work items across projects, and move cards on the Kanban board.
                See <a href="Azd-Boards.topic"/>.</li>
            <li><b>Metrics dashboards:</b> pipeline and pull request metrics, queue time statistics, and an agent pool view with agent actions.
                See <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Metrics.topic"/>.</li>
            <li><b>Queue time:</b> run details show how long a run waited for an agent.</li>
            <li><b>Auto-refresh:</b> separate settings for pipelines and pull requests.</li>
            <li><b>Sort popups:</b> the pull request and pipeline lists have a sort button.</li>
            <li><b>Android Studio:</b> the stage diagram and the metrics dashboards work in Android Studio.</li>
            <li><b>Corporate proxies:</b> AZD retries requests that a TLS-inspecting proxy interrupts instead of asking for a new token.</li>
            <li><b>Built-in AI provider:</b> the AZD provider uses GPT-5.4 mini and works without setup.</li>
        </list>

        <chapter title="Pipeline approvals" id="pipeline-approvals">
            <p>
                Approve, reject or defer environment approvals and <code>ManualValidation@1</code> tasks from the run tab, and get notified when a run waits for you.
                See <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Approvals.topic"/>.
            </p>
            <img src="approva_bottom.png" alt="Run tab with the Awaiting for approval banner, a Comment field and the Approve and Reject buttons"
                 width="512" border-effect="rounded"/>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Pipeline test results" id="pipeline-tests">
            <p>
                The <control>Tests</control> tab shows a summary of the run's tests and sorts them by name or duration.
                Associate automated tests with Azure DevOps test cases from the context menu.
                See <a href="Azd-Pipeline-Tests.topic"/>.
            </p>
            <img src="pipeline_test_results_v2.png"
                 alt="Run tab next to the Tests tab with the test summary and a tree of test classes"
                 width="706" thumbnail="true" border-effect="rounded"/>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="AI log analysis" id="log-analysis">
            <p>
                Stage logs open in the editor page by page.
                <control>Chat with AI About This Log</control> sends a log to an AI provider that explains the failure and answers follow-up questions.
                See <a href="Azure-DevOps-Pipelines.topic" anchor="analyze-logs-with-ai">Analyze a log with AI</a>.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Pull request metrics" id="azd_pr_metrics">
            <p>
                A dashboard shows pull request cycle time, throughput and review activity for the repository.
                See <a href="Work-with-Azure-DevOps-pull-requests.topic" anchor="pr-metrics">Pull request metrics</a>.
            </p>
        </chapter>

        <chapter title="Pull requests" id="pr-improvements-2026-1">
            <list>
                <li>Commit links in the timeline open the commit in the pull request details.</li>
                <li><code>@</code> mentions and <code>!</code> pull request references autocomplete in comments.</li>
                <li>A toggle shows or hides draft pull requests.</li>
                <li>An expired build in the CI status popup can be queued again.</li>
                <li>The <a href="AI-Pull-Request-Review.topic">AI review tour</a> walks you through the changes.</li>
            </list>
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

